BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Quiet Your Mind and Open Your Heart with Sha Hurley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T163000
UID:260727Mq60RVKDdE6qudr1ys6S0A
DESCRIPTION:Quiet your mind\, and open your heart – A guided journey to 
 cultivate inner peace\, joy\, and freedom. Treat yourself to a day of nour
 ishment\, meditation\, creative self-expression \\(drawing\\)\, yoga\, and
  sound bath on our forested sanctuary grounds. In the morning\, join Sha o
 n a guided journey of meditation\, creative self- expression\, yoga/moveme
 nt\, and sound bath in nature that intends to support you: \n\nslowing dow
 n\, releasing\, and renewing\n\nconnecting to inner stillness and clarity\
 n\ncleansing your emotional body\n\nletting go of self-sabotaging patterns
 \n\nremembering and embodying your essence\n\nconnecting to yourself\, nat
 ure\, and like-minded souls in a non-judgmental space\n\nAfter the morning
  workshop\, a nourishing lunch will be offered in a magical creekside sett
 ing beneath the shade of oak and bay trees. Your afternoon includes a ceda
 r enzyme footbath with guided walking and seated meditations\, your choice
  of a massage or facial and time in our renowned Japanese garden. \n\nAbou
 t your guide Sha Hurley: \n\nSha is all about authenticity and inner well-
 being. Her health\, relationship\, and career crises led her on an inner t
 ransformational journey of self-discovery\, healing\, and mastery. She’s
  been traveling around the world\, learning and teaching at places such as
  Esalen Institute\, Blue Spirit\, and Spirit Rock to dive deeply into the 
 field of human potential and inner child healing.Join Us!
URL:https://osmosis.com/event/quiet-mind-open-heart/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wait Wait… Don't Tell Me!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T073000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T073000
UID:260722MRFKhiQuWE6jJ63yCxaQbw
DESCRIPTION:Wait Wait… Don’t Tell Me! NPR’s Peabody Award-winning co
 medy news quiz show hosted by Peter Sagal Thursday\, July 30 at 7:30 p.m. 
 Weill Hall \\+ Lawn Wait Wait… Don’t Tell Me! is National Public Radio
 ’s Peabody Award-winning comedy news quiz show. Host Peter Sagal leads a
  rotating panel of comedians\, writers\, listener contestants\, and celebr
 ity guests through a rollicking review of the week’s news. Contestants v
 ie for the most coveted prize in all of public radio: a custom-recorded gr
 eeting by any of our cast members for their voicemail. Every week\, Wait\,
  Wait…. Don’t Tell Me! records in front of a live audience\, then care
 fully edits out all the raunchy\, inappropriate\, shocking\, and hilarious
  stuff so we can broadcast something that doesn’t get NPR in trouble… 
 well\, more trouble. The only way you can find out what our panelists and 
 guests really think about the news is to come see for yourself. And please
 —don’t tell NPR. Also\, we’re all much more attractive than we sound
 . Supported in part by Cartograph Wines. Info and tickets at https://gmc.s
 onoma.edu/wait-wait-dont-tell-me
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/988887567048769/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
