BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Harvest Cooking: Learn and Lunch with Stephanie Klassen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T130000
UID:260729eV0ctS7_Y0GzOA7L9c70BQ
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the flavors of the Mediterranean with this relaxed s
 ummer lunch menu. Learn how to make the most of your backyard or farmer's 
 market bounty with this demonstration class taught by local cookbook autho
 r Stephanie Klassen.\n\nShe'll show you how to turn those overflowing bask
 ets of summer veggies into a cool Summer Garden Gazpacho\, a colorful Prov
 encal Vegetable Galette and Green Bean-Feta Salad. (And don't forget Nonna
 's Olive Oil Cookies for dessert!) After the demo\, we'll sit down togethe
 r for an al fresco lunch overlooking our beautiful organic orchards.\n\nWh
 at to Expect:\n\n\\*A hands-on cooking demonstration in our charming Apple
  Cottage kitchen\n\n\\*Expert tips from Stephanie on creating delicious di
 shes using fresh\, local produce\n\n\\*A sit-down lunch featuring the dish
 es you just watched being made\, enjoyed at a table overlooking our apple 
 orchard\n\n\\*A signature refreshment: citrus shrub\, freshly pressed appl
 e cider or apple cider spritz\\*\n\nA scenic ride in our apple-themed trol
 ley from the Farm Shop to the Apple Cottage\n\n\\*10% off all Farm Shop pu
 rchases on the day of the class\n\nStephanie Klassen is the author of seve
 n cookbooks\, including A Little Taste of San Francisco and Honey from Flo
 wer to Table. She has taught seasonal cooking at farmers markets and other
  venues from Brooklyn to Berkeley\, including the Ferry Plaza Farmers' Mar
 ket in San Francisco and the Gravenstein Apple Fair in Sebastopol. She has
  cooked at numerous artists' and writers' retreats including the Headlands
  Center for the Arts in Sausalito\, and studied organic farming at the Cen
 ter for Agrocology at UC Santa Cruz.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/616831/summ
 er-harvest-cooking-learn-and-lunch-with-stephanie-klassen
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Back pOrchEstra at Petaluma Theatre Square Plaza\, Fri. eve. July 
 31 6:00pm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T200000
UID:260728Ur4X_qpR5Eawjh8z9bXe1g
DESCRIPTION:Back pOrchEstra at Petaluma Theatre Square Plaza\, Fri. eve. J
 uly 31\, 6:00-8:00 pm\n\n...with Candy Girard\, Gary Potterton\, Luis Rodr
 iguez\, Jen Rund and Tim Eschliman\n\n101 Second St\, Petaluma\, CA 94952\
 n\nOutdoor event\, we'll have plenty roots rock\, cajun\, 2-beat\, western
  swing and country blues originals and historic numbers... on resonator gu
 itar\, violin\, bass\, drums & electric guitar.\n\nWe have a single out!: 
 https://orcd.co/lxz1l6v "I'm Wild About My Lovin'"\, celebrating the new "
 Stories In The Heart" album\, hear the whole thing now!: https://orcd.co/5
 xga7nr\n\n"...What sets 'Stories In The Heart' apart is its sense of balan
 ce. Resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\, drums\, percussion\, dobro\, and Te
 lecaster create a flexible\, roots-forward palette that allows Back Porche
 stra to move between styles fluidly. The songs echo traditions without ree
 nacting them\, keeping one foot in the past and the other firmly planted i
 n the present." - Vince's Hot Picks (Best of 2026) New Releases Now\n\n"Th
 e guitars slam like saloon doors\, the violin traces lines that oscillate 
 between melancholy and jubilation\, the rhythm section moves forward with 
 a tranquil groove that never rushes but never falters... Back pOrchEstra d
 elivers a luminous\, earthy\, profoundly human record. An album that makes
  you want to sit on a porch\, watch the sunset\, and let the stories do th
 eir work...." - Fred Delforge\, Zicazine (translated from French)\n\nBack 
 pOrchEstra is a compact Shelter-in-Place-inspired musical combo ....going 
 back to the basics... Formed for the first time the locked-down summer of 
 2020. The band draws from new original material as well as reworked classi
 cs by Hank Williams\, Taj Mahal\, Dan Hicks\, Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob Wills
 \, Bobby Charles ...even Christmas Jug Band tunes\n\n... check out the "Du
 sty Road I'm On" video: https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots roc
 k number with a Cajun flavor and hints of Jesse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\
 n\nThe previous single\, the Neo-Motown/Levon Helm style "Ever Think About
  It\," is here: https://orcd.co/qo5579q\n\nLPs\, CDs\, and USB-Music Cards
  available all over\, including https://www.globerecords.com\n\nmore at...
  https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://backporchestra.bandca
 mp.com\n\nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0d
 EI-7hlpI8nr7apiNf\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/backporchestra.bsky
 .social\n\nReverb Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/backporchestra\n\nF
 acebook: https://www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nInstagram: https://ww
 w.instagram.com/backporchestra/\n\n#rootsrock\n\n#americanrootsmusic\n\n#a
 mericanamusic\n\n#rockabillymusic\n\n#twangyguitar\n\n#backporchestra\n\n#
 acousticmusic\n\n#adultalbumalternative\n\n#singersongwriter\n\n#folkmusic
 \n\n#folkrock
LOCATION:Theater Square Plaza
URL:https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com/shows.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Social Contractors: Return To Rock Spancky's Bar!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T000000
UID:2607283mTJYNkpikGX3wPY0OEL8w
DESCRIPTION:*….Get ready for the super-entertaining sounds of local band
  The Social Contractors. They totally rock\, in all the right ways…”*
  - Argus-Courier\, 2025\n\nThe Social Contractors return to rock Spancky'
 s Bar from 9 PM until midnight with their upbeat blend of original rock an
 d tasteful interpretations of classic 60-90s hits from the bands you know 
 and love (Beatles\, Hendrix\, Pink Floyd\, Cream\, Stevie Wonder\, Steve M
 iller\, Foreigner\, Police\, Men At Work\, Steely Dan\, Tom Petty\, Tears 
 For Fears\, U2\, and more).\n\nWhether you like melodic vocals\, searing g
 uitar and sax solos\, intriguing lyrics\, captivating songs\, or just grea
 t dynamic and danceable rhythms\, The Social Contractors won't disappoint.
 \n\nThe Social Contractors lineup for this free live performance features 
 band founder and songwriter\, Jason E Davies (lead vocals/lead guitar)\, T
 ravis Thayer (sax/keys/vocals)\, Rob Neidel (bass/vocals)\, and Chris (dru
 ms).
LOCATION:Spancky's Bar
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-social-contractors-
 return-to-rock-spancky-s-bar/19475441/2026-07-31T21
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Max Vogel + The Pickups
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T210000
UID:2607283Rxt4lu2Ik6RBGyB2IIO1A
DESCRIPTION:Max Vogel is a country artist from Windsor\, California\, who 
 has been singing and playing music his entire life. He picked up a guitar 
 at 15 years old and hasn’t put it down since\, spending years honing his
  craft as a singer\, songwriter\, and performer.\n\nInspired by artists li
 ke Garth Brooks\, Alan Jackson\, Randy Travis\, Eric Church\, Zac Brown Ba
 nd\, and Brooks & Dunn\, Max blends traditional country roots with a moder
 n edge. His music is built on honest storytelling\, strong melodies\, and 
 the kind of songs that bring people together.\n\nAfter many years performi
 ng as a solo artist\, Max recently joined forces with a talented group of 
 musicians to form Max Vogel & the Pickups. Together\, they bring a high-en
 ergy country show filled with heartfelt originals\, crowd-favorite country
  anthems\, and a genuine connection with every audience they play for.\n\n
 With a passion for music\, family\, and community\, Max continues carving 
 his path in the country music scene while keeping the spirit of country mu
 sic alive everywhere the band plays.\n\nSeth Burgess teaches popular two-s
 tep and popular western swing dance lessons in the Santa Rosa area. He reg
 ularly hosts multi-week\, progressive dance series and community workshops
  at the historic Alexander Valley Community Hall in Geyserville. \n\nHis 
 classes focus on traditional\, boot-scootin' partner dancing rather than l
 ine dancing\, making them a great way to prep for local social events.\n\n
 All Ages\n\n$15
LOCATION:Rio Nido Roadhouse
URL:https://www.rionidoroadhouse.com/calendar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
