BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jessie Laura Artist Exhibition + Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T180000
UID:2607202gjidyxe80K34yk6yFhhyw
DESCRIPTION:In At the Threshold\, San Francisco-based artist Jessie Laura 
 presents a new body of stitched paintings and canvas collages that examine
  the boundary between the physical world and the transcendental one. \n\n
 Laura builds her surfaces through staining\, stitching\, and layering\, ab
 sorbing color directly into raw canvas\, then applying translucent white o
 verlays that partially conceal geometric forms beneath. The raw canvas is 
 not passive ground but active material: its texture\, warmth\, and porosit
 y shape every decision. What remains unpainted is as considered as what is
  stained. \n\nThe works are organized around different color groupings\, 
 shifting in temperature and mood\, evoking the landscape. Architectural in
  their geometry\, the paintings reference the structural logic of Sea Ranc
 h without illustrating it: the diagonal\, the plane\, the threshold betwee
 n inside and outside that defines the site's design philosophy. The white 
 geometric forms that move across each surface act as vessels of light\, a 
 continuation of Laura's earlier white work\, now folded into a field of co
 lor and atmosphere. \n\nSea Ranch was built on the belief that human cons
 truction and natural environment could achieve genuine synthesis. That ide
 al has always lived somewhere between aspiration and fact. Laura's works o
 ccupy the same productive tension: precise in their making\, open in their
  meaning\, suspended between arrival and pursuit. These thresholds are not
  gates to otherworldly visions but modest ruptures\, barely perceptible op
 enings. They invite you to notice the surface\, the process\, the moment j
 ust before transformation. \n\nAt the Threshold is Laura's second solo ex
 hibition at The Sea Ranch Lodge\, following Modernist Utopia in 2024.\n\nO
 n Friday\, 09.11 join us for a conversation with Jessie Laura and Nicole M
 ueller\, artist and cohost of the Beyond the Studio podcast. This will be 
 a candid conversation about process\, intuition\, and the quiet space betw
 een making and meaning. Set against the backdrop of Laura's exhibition At 
 The Threshold\, the work itself becomes the starting point of this convers
 ation.\n\nAbout The Artist: Jessie Laura (b. 1987\, Lima\, Peru) is a Peru
 vian visual artist and creative director based in San Francisco. Working p
 rimarily in mixed media\, her practice moves between collage\, relief\, an
 d stitched painting\, using geometric abstraction to explore form\, light\
 , and spatial rhythm. Influenced by natural systems and modernist design\,
  she creates compositions that invite slow looking through material restra
 int\, repetition\, and negative space.\n\nLaura studied Film at the School
  of Visual Arts in New York (SVA NYC) and holds a BFA in Design. She has e
 xhibited in solo and group exhibitions throughout the U.S. and Japan\, com
 pleted residencies at Rule Gallery in Marfa\, Texas\, and Art Warehouse in
  Delray Beach\, Florida\, and her work has been featured by Hyperallergic\
 , Artsy\, Apartment Therapy\, and as The Other Art Fair's Director's Pick 
 (2023). Her work is held in private and corporate collections in the U.S. 
 and U.K.\n\nwww.jessie-laura.com\n\n@jessie.laura.artwork
LOCATION:Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/jessie-laura-artist-exh
 ibition-reception/19430379/2026-07-31T16
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
