BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The MAC FREE August 1-2 with Bank of America Museums on Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T170000
UID:260728k1i3vegMnkSfk9Ezrg-HdA
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is August 1-2. \n\nLooking for a chance to squeeze the last d
 rop out of summer and beat the heat? The “MAC” \\(Napa Valley Museum o
 f Art & Culture\\) has exciting exhibits including My Andy: Photographs by
  Victoria Wyeth. Victoria\, the only grandchild of Andrew and Betsy Wyeth\
 , comes from a long lineage of painters\, but chose photography. In the wo
 rks on display for this exhibit\, Victoria assiduously captured moments in
  her grandfather’s life—both intimate and spontaneous—that show a ma
 n at ease with himself and his family. She depicts his unique ability to i
 nhabit the enchanted worlds he created. Victoria’s work is presented at 
 The MAC as a companion to the exhibition “The Wyeths: Three Generations 
 | Works from the Bank of America Collection\,” complimenting and informi
 ng the paintings and drawings of her family. \n\nBank of America Museums 
 on Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first full week
 end of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Privat
 e Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of America\
 , Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID for access
 . \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https://about.b
 ankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum of Art and Culture
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
