DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 1\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation
 \n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\
 n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$110\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\
 n$25\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$135\n\nJoin guest Bay Area artist\, B
 ettina Pauly in a special one-day workshop in learning how to use differen
 t materials to create a printmaking plate for a pasta machine using water 
 soluble etching inks. Create your own prints using a pasta machine as a pr
 ess!Learn how to revive your manual hand crank pasta maker to make small d
 rypoint fine line prints. This popular technique uses the pressure that n
 ormally rolls out pasta dough to print artwork instead! Students will enga
 ge with milk cartons\, Tetra Paks\, and Akua plate material. Learn how to 
 properly ink up the plate\, add packing to the pasta maker for the perfect
  impression\, and pull prints to make a small format 4 x 6 edition that ca
 n be produced multiple times. The instructor will demonstrate how easy it 
 is to use and clean a pasta machine so using it for pasta AND printing can
  be an option. Prints will be made using a drypoint needle and a cutting k
 nife\, and will be printed on Rives BFK paper with oil-based etching inks.
  This will be a day of fun experimentation in printmaking!The materials fe
 e includes\; drypoint needle\, chipboard\, felt and printing papers that s
 tudents will be able to take home to continue making prints on their own p
 asta machines. Please note: This class requires some hand dexterity to ma
 neuver the etching tools and pasta machine. Participants should feel comfo
 rtable using tools with sharp edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/pasta-machine-printing/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art FREE August 1-2 Bank of America Museum
 s on Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T170000
UID:260728Keh3iIhnFkOS3k3nDOHLVw
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is August 1-2. \n\nLooking for a chance to squeeze the last d
 rop out of summer and beat the heat? The Sonoma Valley Museum of Art has e
 xciting exhibits including John Paul Morabito: Dancing in the Night\, feat
 uring colorful weaving\, and Norma I. Quintana: Paradise of Memory / Para
 íso de la Memoria\, a portrait series linking memory with community ident
 ity. Inspired by portraits created by itinerant photographers in Puerto Ri
 co\, her images honor everyday lives as a vital part of cultural remembran
 ce. These “jewels of memory” capture not just faces\, but also the tra
 ces of experience that bind people across generations.\n\nBank of America 
 Museums on Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first f
 ull weekend of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of Americ
 a Private Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of 
 America\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID fo
 r access. \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https:/
 /about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Sonoma Valle Museum of Art
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Experience (Jimi Hendrix tribute) with The Old Souls: Blues Ex
 periment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T230000
UID:260728A2wQXokkn0yQxFhveSDSMg
DESCRIPTION:THE EXPERIENCE are Sonoma County's brand new favorite power tr
 io! They carry the torch of Jimi's passionate music into 2026 and beyond. 
 Featuring George Marshall (guitar)\, Dave Hawkey (bass)\, and Gregg Wilter
 mood (drums).\n\nWith special guests:\n\nThe Old Souls: Blues Experiment *
 *https://remimoulder.com/the-old-souls-1** Founded by Remi Moulder\, The O
 ld Souls: Blues Experiment is a high-voltage preservation of electric blue
 s built on a foundation of deep audience connection and charismatic showma
 nship. This diverse collective of young musicians is dedicated to keeping 
 the fire of electric blues-rock alive\, blending the raw energy of modern 
 youth with the timeless grit of the masters.\n\nOur mission is simple: to 
 prove that the blues isn't a museum piece—it’s a living\, breathing\, 
 and electric force. We’ve spent our lives chasing the sounds of legends 
 like B.B. King\, Eric Clapton\, Stevie Ray Vaughan\, and Joe Bonamassa\, r
 eimagining that legacy for a new generation.\n\nDoors 7pm | Show 8pm 21+ N
 o cover\n\nBarrel Proof Lounge - 501 Mendocino Ave\, Santa Rosa
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-experience-jimi-hendrix-tribute-with-
 the-old-souls-blues-experiment-tickets-1995696073679?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
