SUMMARY:Sugarloaf New Volunteer Orientation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T150000
UID:260711K6XG0i9ni0C_jKHyNxxn1Q
DESCRIPTION:When you join Sugarloaf's 200\\+ member volunteer commu
 nity\, you gain access to a whole new appreciation for your loc
 al State Park. Make meaningful connections with fellow volunteers\
 , learn new skills\, enjoy time outdoors in a beautiful setting\
 , and play an integral role in keeping Sugarloaf Ridge State Pa
 rk open and accessible for everyone.\n\n Join us at our next vo
 lunteer orientation Sunday April 26\, 2026 from 1:00- 3:00 pmto 
 learn what it takes to steward a state park! We'll cover the h
 istory of Sugarloaf\, how Sonoma Ecology Center operates the park
 \, and the various volunteer opportunities available. Beyond the 
 mandatory initial orientation\, trainings and docent enrichment act
 ivities will take place periodically\, depending on your interests
  and role. \n\nHere are some of the vital ways that volunteers
  support Sugarloaf's operations:\n\nServe as docents at the Visito
 r Center\n\nDirect visitors at the entrance kiosk\n\nAssist with d
 ata collection and entry\, like our extensive Critter Cam wildlif
 e tracking project\n\nAid project research and grant-writing\n\nWork
  on trail and park maintenance projects\n\nFacilitate special even
 ts and parking\n\nSpanish/English literacy and conversational fluenc
 y is a plus\n\nView more volunteer opportunities and specifics in
  our website. Experience is not necessary but welcomed\, as well
  as a willingness to learn and the desire to share that knowle
 dge with our visitors. We ask for a minimum commitment of 4 ho
 urs per month.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/sugarloaf-new-volunteer-orientation-812026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Keys to Health\, Peace\, and Freedom - A Presentation by Dr Wi
 ll Tuttle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T150000
UID:260710AIVfVNCtI0aENJIoUr_ZXA
DESCRIPTION:Are you concerned about the quality of food available today?\n
 \nAre you troubled by the high rates of chronic disease in our society?\n\
 nWould you like to understand the hidden roots of the dilemmas we face as 
 individuals and a society\, and to learn new skills for healthier\, more s
 ustainable living?\n\nAre you interested in practical keys to radiant heal
 th?\n\nAuthor of international best-seller\, The World Peace Diet\, as wel
 l as the companion books The World Peace Way and Food for Freedom\, Dr. Wi
 ll Tuttle delivers an inspiring talk about our culture’s food systems an
 d shares his wisdom regarding practical tools to reduce our environmental 
 footprint\, make healthy lifestyle choices\, and improve our relationships
 \, with one another and the world. Dr. Tuttle and his spouse Madeleine wil
 l guide us toward building radiant health\, optimizing our wellness and jo
 y\, and building a positive future for all. DIscover the knowledge for sel
 f-healing\, physically\, socially\, culturally\, psychologically\, and spi
 ritually!\n\nQ & A session and discussion to follow. Don't miss the chance
  to get your signed copies of The World Peace Diet and The World Peace Way
  - books will be for sale with the author available for signing.\n\nDr Wil
 l Tuttle\, visionary educator\, musician\, and author of the international
  best-seller\, The World Peace Diet\, published in 16 languages\, has lect
 ured and performed in over 50 countries. A featured expert in Cowspiracy a
 nd other documentary films\, he’s a recipient of the prestigious Courage
  of Conscience Award. A former Zen monk and Dharma Master in the Zen tradi
 tion\, he is the author of several books and has created 10 much-loved CD 
 albums of original piano music. His inspiring presentations often include 
 his music as well as evocative animal and nature paintings by his spouse\,
  Madeleine\, visionary artist from Switzerland\, who is also a flutist\, W
 aldorf teacher\, organic gardener\, and vegan chef. Visit www.worldpeaced
 iet.com to learn more about their work.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/616129/the-
 keys-to-health-peace-and-freedom-a-presentation-by-dr-will-tuttle
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wear + Share + Repair ✨ CLOTHING SWAP!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T140000
UID:260709fFLMgydYo0OTF3MY6FGgxw
DESCRIPTION:**Community Clothing Swap @ Art Escape**\n\nJoin us for a rela
 xed\, drop-in clothing swap this summer at Art Escape!\n\nBring clothes yo
 u no longer wear\, set them out on our tables or tarps\, and swap them for
  something new-to-you. No registration needed—and you don’t have to br
 ing anything to participate.\n\nInside\, we’ll also have a **DIY Mending
  & Patch Bar + Dye Station** open all day. Fix\, alter\, or customize your
  swapped items with sewing machines\, supplies\, and help from experienced
  sewists—all free of charge (donations welcome).\n\n**How it works:**\n\
 nDrop in and check in at the entrance\n\nSet out your clothing\n\nBrowse a
 nd swap freely\n\nHead upstairs to mend\, patch\, or personalize your find
 s\n\n**Why come?** It’s a fun\, easy way to build community\, refresh yo
 ur wardrobe\, and keep clothing out of landfills by giving it a second lif
 e.
LOCATION:Art Escape
URL:https://artescapesonoma.jumbula.com/Summer2026/WearShareRepairCLOTHING
 SWAP
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STEAM UP! Sturgeons Mill Historic Steam Powered Sawmill!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T150000
UID:260707Fsp9UtEcnEanMNusLJc_TA
DESCRIPTION:Steam Up! Sturgeons Mill\, a 100 yr old Historic Steam Powered
  Sawmill will open its gates Aug. 1 & 2 for our Public Demonstration Weeke
 nd. Watch the historic working museum come to life as redwood logs are mil
 led into lumber and slabs. Enjoy the sweet smell of wood smoke and plumes 
 of steam as they are hurled skyward and the sounds of the sawmill radiate 
 throughout a secluded redwood canyon. Docent tours will lead you through C
 alifornia Sawmill History as you venture the beautiful grounds of the sawm
 ill and woodland gardens. Open 10:00 - 3:00 each day with lunch available 
 to purchase in our beautiful picnic grounds while listening to a local Uku
 lele Band. Free\, donations appreciated as we are a all volunteer non-prof
 it organization. For more info visit our website\, Sturgeonsmill.com.
LOCATION:Sturgeons Mill
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/steam-up-sturgeons-mill
 -historic-steam-powered-sawmill/19350092/2026-08-01T10
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
