BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T180000
UID:260715auDfmCbc8E6yMB5LuGB-6w
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\nAUGUST EXHIBIT: PAINT
 ING IN FAUVE\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  July 27 – August 30\, 2026\n\nRECEPTION
 : SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow LaLand and G
 en Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to t
 ake part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by
  a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma wine country a
 rtist\, Willow LaLand presents Painting in Fauve\, a collection of oil and
  acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant beauty through the a
 rtist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realistic landscapes\, these
  works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, tapping into the wild
  Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\, “Mt. Tamalpais
 ” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over its undulating slo
 pes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mountain’s grandeu
 r.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with color as it overloo
 ks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us from palette to palat
 e as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine red wine in “Somme
 lier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\, LaLand notes “
 I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in color\, and give a t
 angible realistic impression within a completely fantastical expression.
 ”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her studies as a young g
 irl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspired by early Ame
 rican realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve dramatic realism
 .  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful response to her 
 themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love both her styles a
 nd have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing between the two
 .  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, and participated 
 in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American Art Collector ma
 gazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: LaLand will host t
 he Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n
 \nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Gen Zorich’s Summertime\, hi
 ghlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth of long\, lazy summer
  days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist and environmental scien
 tist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understanding of the natural w
 orld. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating on pastel pads in “S
 ummer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy days.  These works wou
 ld bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of year.  An award-winn
 ing artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has been a longtime participa
 nt in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet the artist: Zorich wil
 l host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, August 4\, 11am to 6 pm
  and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEALDSBUR
 G\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st
  Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creati
 vity with over 20 galleries participating. This month’s special theme: M
 usic and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306
  Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 1
 1am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T180000
UID:260715LCtmQfJMtECDN7hYvJCjKA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\n**AUGUST EXHIBIT: PAI
 NTING IN FAUVE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **July 27 – August 30\, 2026**\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow La
 Land and Gen Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be
  sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautif
 ul work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma wi
 ne country artist\, **Willow LaLand** presents **Painting in Fauve\,** a c
 ollection of oil and acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant 
 beauty through the artist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realisti
 c landscapes\, these works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, t
 apping into the wild Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\
 , “Mt. Tamalpais” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over 
 its undulating slopes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mo
 untain’s grandeur.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with c
 olor as it overlooks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us fro
 m palette to palate as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine re
 d wine in “Sommelier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\
 , LaLand notes “I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in co
 lor\, and give a tangible realistic impression within a completely fantast
 ical expression.”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her stud
 ies as a young girl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspi
 red by early American realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve 
 dramatic realism.  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful 
 response to her themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love b
 oth her styles and have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing
  between the two.  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, a
 nd participated in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American 
 Art Collector magazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: La
 Land will host the Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\,
  11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Gen Zorich
 ’s Summertime\,** highlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth
  of long\, lazy summer days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist a
 nd environmental scientist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understa
 nding of the natural world. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating 
 on pastel pads in “Summer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy d
 ays.  These works would bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of
  year.  An award-winning artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has bee
 n a longtime participant in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Zorich will host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, A
 ugust 4\, 11am to 6 pm and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE
  Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event 
 celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. This 
 month’s special theme: Music and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 43
 1-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
