BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing Trees in Mixed Media at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T140000
UID:260720rMM2UEffAECvmpw6aJrkfw
DESCRIPTION:Spend a day immersed in the art of drawing trees\, set against
  the inspiring landscape of Jack London State Historic Park. This plein ai
 r workshop blends skill-building with outdoor observation\, helping you de
 epen both your technique and your connection to the natural world.\n\nIn t
 he morning\, focus on foundational drawing principles—learning how to ca
 pture accurate proportions\, simplify complex forms\, and develop a strong
  sense of value.\n\nIn the afternoon\, attention shifts to the expressive 
 qualities of trees\, exploring texture\, color\, and light as observed dir
 ectly from the landscape. Enhance your drawings with watercolor washes\, a
 dding depth\, atmosphere\, and color to bring trees to life. Step-by-step 
 guidance ensures that finished piece reflects both structure and character
 .\n\nBring a picnic lunch for a mid-day break\, and a lightweight folding 
 chair if you have one (seating is also available at picnic tables\, benche
 s\, or on the ground). All materials are provided.  Artists of all experi
 ence levels are welcome.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/plein-air-trees-august-2026-copy-cop
 y/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ruta a los Secuoyas - Una Caminata en Español
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T130000
UID:260720nfoJOtMOFUSUvaC6nqArkw
DESCRIPTION:¿Sabía que la especie de árbol más alta del mundo crece en
  Sonoma Mountain? Hace unos doscientos años\, la zona de Glen Ellen estab
 a rodeada de enormes secuoyas de más de mil años de antigüedad. Hoy en 
 día\, todavía se pueden ver algunos de estos árboles en diversas partes
  del parque: vestigios de aquellos gigantes.\n\nEn esta caminata —guiada
  en español—\, las secuoyas más grandes del valle de Sonoma ofrecerán
  refugio frente al sol del verano. El grupo explorará la biología de est
 os árboles y aprenderá cómo resisten el calor. La excursión también i
 ncluirá una visita al árbol más grande del parque.\n\n/ / /\n\nDid you 
 know that the world's tallest tree species grows on Sonoma Mountain? About
  two hundred years ago\, the Glen Ellen area was surrounded by massive red
 woods that were over a thousand years old. Today\, some of these trees can
  still be seen in various parts of the park—remnants of those giants.\n\
 nOn this hike – guided in Spanish - the largest redwoods in Sonoma Valle
 y will provide shelter from the summer sun. The group will explore the bio
 logy of these trees and learn how they withstand the heat. This hike will 
 also include a visit to the park’s largest tree.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/ruta-a-las-secuoyas-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
