DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T160000
UID:2607131nCDJZEMK0KIkuBDYMnu1A
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on using a hollander beater and creating
  beautiful paper that can be used for drawing\, painting\, and even printm
 aking. This class will begin by focusing on processing a selection of fibe
 rs to make Western European style paper. After using a Hollander beater to
  break down these fibers\, we will make numerous sheets of paper and explo
 re ways to sheet form\, followed by an in-depth conversation around drying
  techniques. Looking at paper through a historical lens\, we will also tal
 k about the importance of creating unique substrates and discuss ways of b
 ringing hand papermaking into a variety of studio practices and set-ups. M
 aterials: All materials included in registration fee. Available Dates Satu
 rday\, August 8th 11:00am - 4:00pm
