BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx-Beginner Hiking for Fitness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T130000
UID:260701MLb4MKAAP0W1D-tqvSKtIg
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this fitness program\, where the leaders w
 ill guide you on a series of 8 weekly hikes with the challenge
  increasing each week. Before the first hike\, the leader will 
 discuss proper shoes\, hydration\, incorporating hiking poles\, pro
 per pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for the long rout
 e up Brushy Peaks Trail\, where hikers can enjoy the beautiful 
 vistas.\n\nThe following is a list of possible routes selected fo
 r this hiking series: 1\\) Sat 8/1 - White Barn to Uranus\, 2.1
  miles\, 180 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 2\\) Sat 8/8 - Me
 adow- Hillside loop\, 3 miles\, 490 ft elev \\[meet @ white bar
 n\\] 3\\) Sat 8/15 - Lake Ralphine & Spring Lake loop\, 4.3 mil
 es\, 420 ft elev \\[meet @ Howarth Park's Boathouse\\] 4\\) Sat 
 8/22- Jack London State Historic Park\, May’s Clearing\, 3.5 mi
 les\, 820 ft elev \\[meet @ upper parking lot\, 2400 London Ran
 ch Road\, Glen Ellen\, CA 95442\\] 5\\) Sat 8/29 - Vista Trail 
 loop\, 3.5 miles\, 830 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 6\\) Sat
  9/5 – Stern \\+ Waterfall loop\, 2.7 miles\, 750 ft elev \\
 [meet @ main lot\\] 7\\) Sat 9/12 – Sonoma Valley Regional Par
 k & Lake Suttonfield loop\, 4.3\, miles\, 770 ft elev \\[meet a
 t Valley of the Moon Trailhead on Arnold Dr.\\] 8\\) Sat 9/19 
 – Hillside to Neptune picnic table\, 4.4 miles\, 970 ft elev 
 \\[meet @ white barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes or dates are
  subject to change depending on logistics. Wear appropriate footw
 ear for rocky/slippery trails and layers. Bring at least a quart
  \\(32oz\\) of water\, and if desired\, a snack. The group will
  be limited to 35 participants.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/beghffsummer26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T143000
UID:260626TPCBWJFQmEGz4u8wOWkycg
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\n*White Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil*\n\nSu
 sanna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\
 n*Bliss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish*\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nH
 eirloom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\n*Smoked Bacon-Grain Must
 ard Dressing*\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian 
 Seven-Spiced Chicken Breast\n\n*Indonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable
  Ragout\, Balado Sauce*\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Van
 illa Burnt Basque Cheesecake\n\n*Raspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licori
 ce-Poached Cherries*\n\n*Brown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime*\n\n**Es
 tate Ingredients:**\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, L
 emons\, Olive Oil\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tom
 atoes\, Zucchini and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservat
 ions are required. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate 
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Live Music at Spicy Vines feat. Adam Lieb
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T180000
UID:260605OaQTHdbXX0SZfxyQt4GIyA
DESCRIPTION:*Where unforgettable wines\, live music\, and good vibes come 
 together.*\n\nJoin us every Saturday from 3–6 PM at Spicy Vines for a ta
 sting room experience like no other — where top local musicians from acr
 oss the Bay Area meet our award-winning small-lot wines. From Rock & Roll 
 and Blues to Jazz\, Bluegrass\, and Americana\, each weekend brings new so
 unds and new reasons to raise a glass. \n\n**Adam Lieb**\n\nBlending rock
 \, blues\, soul\, and global folk influences\, singer-songwriter and guita
 rist Adam Lieb delivers music infused with passion\, craftsmanship\, and
  deep cultural roots.\n\n **Details**\n\nNo cover. Walk-ins are welcome\,
  but this event tends to fill up quickly\, so we recommend making a reserv
 ation. We are dog and family friendly!
LOCATION:Spicy Vines Winery
URL:https://spicyvines.com/event/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Paddle The Petaluma: Turn to The River" Guided Kayak Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T120000
UID:260514VKwcPEzJPESbsb_ZK4T7-Q
DESCRIPTION:Paddle the Petaluma: Turn to The River is a relaxed\, beginner
 -friendly guided kayak tour exploring the past\, present\, and future of P
 etaluma’s historic waterway. Launching right from downtown at The Floath
 ouse Petaluma\, you'll take part in this Sonoma County Signature Experienc
 e by spending about 90 minutes on the water in stable sit-on-top kayaks\, 
 traveling a gentle mile-and-a-half route through “Petaluma’s Longest P
 ark.”\n\nAlong the way\, you’ll raft up at docks around town\, fascina
 ting  landmarks\, and riverfront gathering spaces to hear stories about h
 ow this Gold Rush-era “saltwater highway” helped shape Petaluma—and 
 how today’s community is continuing to reinvent and reconnect with the r
 iver. This isn’t just a history tour. You’ll also learn about the peop
 le\, businesses\, artists\, nonprofits\, and river advocates helping shape
  the waterway’s future right now.\n\nEverything is included in the $75 e
 xperience: kayak\, gear\, knowledgeable local guides\, insider river stori
 es\, and post-paddle perks at nearby businesses. Finish with plenty of tim
 e for brunch\, coffee\, shopping\, or simply hanging out downtown by the w
 ater. No experience necessary.\n\nNote: The Floathouse Petaluma is a nonpr
 ofit project dedicated to “putting butts in boats and smiles on faces”
  by offering year-round easy access to the Petaluma River in and on people
 -powered water craft through rentals\, events\, classes\, lessons and summ
 er camps.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bricoleur Vineyards Essentials Picnic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T153000
UID:260508nGzTqPUERka2bjBZhOigCA
DESCRIPTION:Bricoleur Vineyards’ beloved Essentials Picnic pairs a b
 ottle of wine with charcuterie\, presented in a quintessential wicker bask
 et and a chic red wagon\, offering a relaxed and beautifully curated alfre
 sco wine country experience. Guests can enjoy their picnic in picturesque\
 , family- and dog-friendly settings across the estate—whether on the Pav
 ilion lawn\, beneath the trellis by the pond\, or at the picnic tables nes
 tled within the culinary and rose gardens. With exceptional wines\, thou
 ghtfully crafted foods\, and sweeping vistas\, a visit to Bricoleur Vin
 eyards offers a laid-back\, family-friendly atmosphere featuring lawn ga
 mes\, board games\, scavenger hunts\, and catch-and-release fishing.
LOCATION:Bricoleur Vineyard
URL:https://bricoleurvineyards.com/pages/visit?srsltid=AfmBOoq4MRc2MHal1tH
 0HwUmLbCHlVrPlsnizqNwrRFitw3UKui4rRJV
