BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Revolutionary Afternoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T160000
UID:260728h6eWHVnudEqUWGbspXJQSQ
DESCRIPTION:An America 250! Tea featuring **Dr. Emily Sneff\,** author of
  *When the Declaration of Independence Was News.*\n\nJoin us for an elega
 nt afternoon of tea and history as we welcome **Dr. Emily Sneff**\, an ea
 rly American historian and nationally recognized expert on the Declaration
  of Independence.\n\nGuests will enjoy **sweet and savory tea fare\, beau
 tifully appointed tables\, and a fascinating presentation** exploring how
  news of American independence spread throughout the colonies and beyond.\
 n\n**About Dr. Sneff:** Joining us from the East Coast\, Dr. Sneff is an e
 arly American historian\, author of *When the Declaration of Independence
  Was News*\, and consulting curator for America 250 exhibitions\, includin
 g projects with Philadelphia's Museum of the American Revolution. Her rese
 arch explores how news of American independence spread throughout the colo
 nies and across the Atlantic in 1776. **www.emilysneff.com**
LOCATION:The Saturday Afternoon Club
URL:https://thesaturdayafternoonclub.com/events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
