END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Then & Now: Faces of the Valley Reception and Film Screening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T193000
UID:260728ZGAntJmgeUepqVOHmhVTfg
DESCRIPTION:This August\, the San Geronimo Valley Community Center in part
 nership with Marin AgeWell Collaborative and Two Valley Community Land Tru
 st a thoughtful series of exhibitions and events exploring aging\, memory\
 , housing\, and the meaning of growing older in community. Centered around
  the traveling exhibit What About Age\, recently shown at the Marin County
  Civic Center\, the series invites residents to reflect on the joys\, chal
 lenges\, and deep connections that come with aging in the San Geronimo and
  Nicasio Valleys.\n\nA special feature of the exhibit will be a companion 
 “Then & Now: Faces of the Valley” photography installation pairing vin
 tage Polaroids taken by the late local photographer Chuck Ford during the 
 Community Center’s Holiday Arts Faire in the 1970s and 1980s with contem
 porary portraits by acclaimed artist photographer Sasha Gulish. Together\,
  the images create an intimate portrait of community members across genera
 tions\, capturing both continuity and change over time. Through photograph
 s\, stories\, and personal reflections\, dozens of local residents share w
 hat it has meant to grow older in this uniquely beautiful and interconnect
 ed rural community.\n\nThe show will open with a reception on Sunday\, Aug
 ust 9th at 4pm and will include a screening of the highly regarded PBS doc
 umentary Lives Well Lived\, a moving film celebrating the wisdom and exper
 iences of adults aged 75 to 100.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/what-abo
 ut-age-then-and-now-faces-of-the-valley-exhibit
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Extended Run: Who Will Dance with Pancho Villa?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T140000
UID:260728YL5R8J2S60mZrSvkrrhUqA
DESCRIPTION:*Who Will Dance with Pancho Villa?* played to sold-out audien
 ces in January. First performed off-Broadway in 1994\, the playwrights upd
 ated the story with the introduction of the **Ballet Folklórico Legado d
 e Mi Alegría de Cloverdale Ca** while developing the play further throug
 h the Raven Players’ ScripTease program. It is the story of a young Chic
 ano from Chicago\, lured to the East Coast by an Ivy League scholarship. A
 s he tries to make a life there\, he neglects family relationships and dee
 p cultural roots established throughout generations. It takes his mother
 ’s nearly fatal heart attack\, help from a Jewish therapist\, and the vi
 sitation of the spirits of his long dead relatives (and of his historical 
 idol\, Pancho Villa) to help him realize what he’s lost\, and how to get
  it back. Dancing spirits\, who are intertwined throughout the play\, help
  remind “Chicano” of the joy in dancing\, especially when dancing is m
 uch more than dancing.\n\nBy John and Gabriel Fraire\n\nDirected by Jenna 
 Vera Dolcini\n\n**August 7\, 8\, 9\, \\*13\, 14\, 15\, 16**\n\n**Friday an
 d Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Matinee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value 
 Thursday:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Admission: Adults:** $25\n\n**Student w/ID:** $1
 0\n\n**\\*Value Thursday Performance:** Pay What You Can
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/who-will-dance-with-pancho-villa-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: P-Butta
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T143000
UID:260728WqNXdr5BeUOoB5lgW1_k0A
DESCRIPTION:Unplug and Groove: P-Butta Live at the Vineyard\n\nJoin us for
  No Cell Sundays with P-Butta\, a local powerhouse trio that's been making
  Sonoma County move for decades.\n\nP-Butta is the instrumental side proje
 ct of the musicians from Rising Tide\, the original Groundation band. With
  Marcus Urani on keyboards\, Ryan Newman on bass\, and Paul Spina on drums
 \, this three-piece brings together four decades of funk\, soul\, and jazz
  mastery that satisfies any musical palate.\n\nExpect to hear groovy cover
 s from legendary artists like The Meters\, Booker T & the M.G.'s\, Herbie 
 Hancock\, Donnie Hathaway\, Cannonball Adderley\, and even the Beastie Boy
 s. Whether you're a jazz head or just love good vibes\, P-Butta delivers t
 he perfect soundtrack for a Sunday afternoon in wine country.\n\nWhat's No
  Cell Sundays?\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your devices\, reconnect wi
 th great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. Check your phone 
 with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting. Bring a blanket\
 , grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
