BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hindsight 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T150000
UID:260728MKgfxGHi-k-MVIwC-KTaJA
DESCRIPTION:The eight playwrights from across the U.S. include local playw
 right Caitlin Strom-Martin\, Arianna Rose\, Rhea MacCallum\, Alan Brooks\,
  Robb Willoughby\, Dan Morra\, Maury Zeff and Steve Koppman. The plays cov
 er topics such as identity\, immigration\, social inequity and the perils 
 of social media\, and include a memory play\, satire\, comedy and drama. H
 indsight Festival plays are performed as staged readings by a talented gro
 up of local actors working with multiple directors. Since its first\, virt
 ual production in 2020\, Hindsight has introduced more than 50 new playwri
 ghts from around the world to local audiences\, earning a reputation for s
 howcasing innovative\, provocative and entertaining scripts. Books of winn
 ing Hindsight play scripts by year are available for sale on Amazon and at
  The California Theatre. Tickets: $17 Advance\, $22 at the Door \\(plus $2
  card processing fee\\) Doors open 12:00pm. Show at 1:00pm.
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/hindsight-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mokuhanga (Ukiyo-e) Japanese Woodblock Printmaking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260809T160000
UID:260728LwVFl0eTj0ad_eA_D98wFw
DESCRIPTION:Weekly every Sundays · 3 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nAugust 9 –
  23\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 4:00 PM Short lunch break included\n\nLocation\
 n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\
 nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$300\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$
 50\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$350\n\nIn this special three-part works
 hop\, participants will be introduced to the art of Japanese woodblock pri
 nting called Ukiyo-E technique. Tomoko Murakami\, an acclaimed Bay Area\, 
 Japanese-born printmaking artist\, will demonstrate the traditional Mokuha
 nga carving and printing process. Tomoko will introduce the relationship b
 etween positive and negative space in relief printing techniques\, includi
 ng Kento registration. Participants will learn to carve their own woodbloc
 ks using Japanese carving tools to create small multi-color woodblocks and
  create prints with non-toxic water-based inks on Japanese paper. Students
  will be able to develop an appreciation of Japanese woodblock prints\, ma
 terials\, processes and innovations. Learn to carve your own woodblocks an
 d create a small edition of multicolor prints! This class is perfect for b
 eginners as well as continuing students. All levels are welcome!Please not
 e: This class requires hand dexterity to maneuver the carving tools. Parti
 cipants should feel comfortable standing and using wood carving tools with
  sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/mokuhanga-japanese-woodbloc
 k-printmaking/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
