UID:260728Pcd4LYrjC0qCO2ST-G6qSA
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Sebastopol Regional Library on Sunday\, June 14\, 2
 026\, at 2:00pm for a conversation about Iran's past\, present\, and futur
 e with Dr. Wendy DeSouza and Dr. Maryam Ghadiri\, followed by a Q&A. Learn
  about Iran today\, the human impact of the ongoing conflict\, and explore
  ways individuals and communities can support the Iranian people and navig
 ate oppressive systems. Dr. Wendy DeSouza is a scholar of Modern Iran and 
 lecturer in Gender and Women's Studies at UC Berkeley and an activist. Dr.
  Maryam Ghadiri is an activist and Organizational Developmental consultant
  at UC Davis\, who grew up in Northern Iran.
