SUMMARY:Beach Bunny & The Beths Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260812T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260812T220000
UID:2607229ZSWcu1k1E-7SuT7kFrRVQ
DESCRIPTION:Beach Bunny & The Beths at Gundlach Bundschu Winery with Suppo
 rt from Wishy – Presented by \\(\\(\\(folkYeah!\\)\\)\\) and Gundlach B
 undschu on Wednesday August 12\, 2026 at 6:00pm at the Gundlach Bundschu A
 mphitheater in Sonoma\, CA. \n\nWHEN: Wednesday\, August 12th 2026 \n\nWHE
 RE: GB Amphitheater \n\nTIME: Doors 5:00pm | Show 6:00pm \n\nBUY TICKETS\n
 \n  \n\nTICKETING: Have your ticket ready when you arrive! If you opted 
 for mobile delivery\, please make sure it’s ready to go on your phone. P
 rinted tickets? Have them out and ready to be scanned. Bacchus Club member
 s\, enjoy express entry with your special line and a complimentary welcome
  splash of wine. \n\nPARKING: Parking is complimentary for Bacchus Wine C
 lub members and available to pre-purchase online. To encourage carpooling\
 , we offer free parking to vehicles with 3\\+ passengers\, full 2-seaters\
 , motorcycles\, and electric vehicles. Otherwise\, parking will be $20 cas
 h at entry. For ADA accommodations please let the parking attendant know a
 nd we encourage contacting us in advance. \n\nPLEASE NO: \n\nCoolers\n\nWa
 ter \\(bring an empty bottle as we have filtered re-fill stations\\)\n\nPe
 ts\n\nChairs\n\nOutside food or drink\n\nBad Attitudes… this is Rhinefa
 rm after all\n\nACCESSIBILITY: For any questions regarding ADA accommodat
 ions related to parking\, seating\, restrooms\, etc. please contact us at
  info@gunbun.com or 707.938.5277. \n\nYOUR EXPERIENCE\, YOUR ADVENTURE:
  At Gundlach Bundschu Winery\, we invite you to immerse yourself in the m
 agic of our outdoor amphitheater\, where the beauty of nature blends with 
 unforgettable performances. As with all great adventures\, attending an ou
 tdoor event carries a touch of unpredictability. \n\nWhether it’s the ru
 stle of the vines in the breeze\, the gentle slope of the hillside\, or th
 e surprises nature has in store\, we encourage you to embrace the moment. 
 While we strive to create a safe and enjoyable environment\, the great out
 doors brings its own set of risks. By joining us\, you understand and acce
 pt the inherent possibilities\, but not limited to\, uneven ground\, chang
 ing weather\, and the occasional visit from our local wildlife. We ask tha
 t you tread carefully\, come prepared for all conditions\, and remember to
  look after yourself and your belongings. \n\nBy attending our events\, yo
 u acknowledge that your participation is voluntary\, and you assume all re
 sponsibility for any personal injuries\, accidents\, or loss of property t
 hat may occur during your time with us. Gundlach Bundschu Winery and its t
 eam are dedicated to your safety\, but cannot be held liable for incidents
  that may arise from the natural elements of this experience. \n\nIn purch
 asing a ticket and joining us under the open sky\, you agree to these term
 s and release Gundlach Bundschu Winery from any claims or liabilities asso
 ciated with the inherent risks of an outdoor gathering. We look forward to
  sharing this special place with you\, where every moment is part of the j
 ourney.
LOCATION:GB Amphitheater
URL:https://www.gunbun.com/event/beach-bunny-the-beths/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rainbow Book Club: Flirting Lessons by Jasmine Guillory
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260812T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260812T180000
UID:2607228nEG7Y2vFEuWPjiI0YraSg
DESCRIPTION:The Rainbow Book Club is cohosted by Mindy from Napa County Li
 brary and Napa Bookmine staff members Kass and Jules. The book club focuse
 s on books that explore and embrace queer identity. This is a free event\,
  but we appreciate your RSVP so we can plan for your attendance! We look f
 orward to welcoming you. ABOUT THE BOOK "The banter zings. The steam rises
  off the pages and the chemistry is sapphic rom-com perfection. These two 
 not only steal each other’s hearts. They’ll steal yours too! Jasmine G
 uillory delivers one of your favorite books of the year!" — Kennedy Ryan
 \, New York Times bestselling author of This Could Be Us “Flirting Lesso
 ns in addition to being a love story between two women\, is a book about h
 ighly competent people battling perfectionism\, surviving interpersonal co
 nflict and trying new things.” — The Washington Post "A lusty queer lo
 ve story by the queen of romance\, herself? Sign me up. With Flirting Less
 ons\, Jasmine Guillory serves up an unforgettable friends-to-lovers journe
 y between buttoned-up Avery and heartbreaker Taylor—and their chemistry 
 is so warm and real\, it catapults off the page. A super-sharp romance for
  the ages!" — Tia Williams\, New York Times bestselling author of A Love
  Song for Ricki Wilde Avery Jensen is almost thirty\, fresh off a breakup\
 , and she’s tired of always being so uptight and well-behaved. She wants
  to get a hobby\, date around \\(especially women\\)\, flirt with everyone
  she sees\, wear something not from the business casual section of her clo
 set—all the fun stuff normal people do in their twenties. One problem: A
 very doesn't know where to start. She doesn't have a lot of dating experie
 nce\, with men or women\, and despite being self-assured at work\, she doe
 sn't have a lot of confidence when it comes to romance. Enter Taylor Camer
 on\, Napa Valley's biggest flirt and champion heartbreaker. Taylor just br
 oke up with her most recent girlfriend\, and her best friend bet her that 
 she can't make it until Labor Day without sleeping with someone. \\(Two wh
 ole months? Without sex? Taylor?!?!\\) So\, she offers to give Avery flirt
 ing lessons. It should keep her busy and stop her from texting people she 
 shouldn't. And it might take her mind off how inadequate she feels compare
 d to her friends\, who all seem much more settled and adult than Taylor. A
 t first\, Avery is stiff and nervous\, but Taylor is patient and encouragi
 ng\, and soon\, Avery looks forward to their weekly lessons. With Taylor
 ’s help\, Avery finally has the life she always wanted. The only issue i
 s: now she wants Taylor. Their attraction becomes impossible to ignore\, d
 espite them both insisting to themselves and everyone else that it isn't s
 erious. When Taylor is forced to confront her feelings for Avery\, she doe
 sn't know what to do—and most importantly\, if she's already ruined the 
 best thing she's ever had. ABOUT THE AUTHOR Jasmine Guillory is a New York
  Times bestselling author. Her novels include Drunk on Love\, The Wedding 
 Date\, the Reese's Book Club selection The Proposal. Her work has appeared
  in The Wall Street Journal\, Cosmopolitan\, Bon Appetit\, and Time. Jasmi
 ne is a frequent book contributor on the Today show. She lives in Oakland\
 , California.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1622479725507363/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
