BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seaweed Foraging (Sonoma Coast) in Bodega Bay
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260814T054500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260814T091500
UID:2605226bHOvQgc30aoGd8z4B1e6Q
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to identify\, use\, and sustainably harvest the bou
 ntiful seaweeds. Harvest up to 10 lbs of seaweed to take home and enjoy. 
 \n\nFrom ancient times to the present\, seaweeds have been used by coastal
  people all over the world to nourish themselves and their gardens\, as w
 ell as for health issues. The Sonoma coast is incredibly rich in seaweeds
  that can be used as food and medicine. \n\nWe will gather on the beach\
 , review some common edible species\, and head to where the sea meets sho
 re to access and appreciate the abundant marine meadow growing on our coas
 t.\n\nThe class also includes community-building activities and will concl
 ude with a cooking demo featuring several varieties of seaweed.  Led by A
 utumn Summers and Ricardo Romero Gianoli\n\nClass Dates (not a series)\n\n
 Fri 6/5 8 am\n\nSat 6/6 8:45 am\n\nFri 6/19 8:15 am\n\nSat 6/20 8:45 am\n\
 nMore dates available in July
LOCATION:Bodega Bay
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/seaweed-foraging-sonoma-coast-in-bodega-b
 ay/2026-06-05/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
