BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pranzo di Ferragosto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T160000
UID:260720468GuVwpTUGbWKFe1PbvwQ
DESCRIPTION:**An Afternoon Italian Style – Celebrating Italian Culture w
 ith Family and Friends** **Benefiting the NBICF Scholarship Fund**\n\nJoin
  us for **Pranzo di Ferragosto** at D'Argenzio Winery as we celebrate on
 e of Italy's most beloved summer traditions. Gather with family and friend
 s on the patio for a memorable afternoon featuring a delicious five-course
  meal of antipasti\, salad\, pasta\, sausage\, and dessert. Wine and other
  beverages will be available for purchase.\n\nIn Italy\, **Ferragosto**\,
  celebrated each year on August 15\, is one of the country's most cherishe
 d holidays. Long communal tables fill town squares and streets as families
  and friends come together to enjoy abundant food\, great conversation\, a
 nd the joy of being together. Rooted in both ancient Roman and religious t
 raditions\, Ferragosto has become a nationwide celebration of summer\, com
 munity\, and Italian hospitality.\n\nWe'll bring that same spirit to Sonom
 a Wine Country—with our own special traditions. Enjoy a friendly bocce b
 all tournament (whether you play or simply cheer from the sidelines)\, bro
 wse our silent auction\, and bid on wonderful prizes while supporting the 
 NBICF Scholarship Fund. Every bid helps preserve and promote Italian herit
 age\, culture\, and language for future generations.\n\nYou'll also have t
 he opportunity to meet some of our scholarship recipients\, hear inspiring
  family stories\, and enjoy live entertainment with Carlo Solivan as we ce
 lebrate the rich traditions that connect us all.\n\nCome hungry\, bring yo
 ur friends and family\, and join us for an unforgettable afternoon of Ital
 ian food\, music\, laughter\, and community.
LOCATION:D'Argenzio Winery
URL:https://nbicf.getcommunal.com/parent_programs/3976
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equality Vines Wine & Donate Benefiting Sonoma Family Meal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T190000
UID:260719JDoy-RBXMEyx5JVBpoaWGQ
DESCRIPTION:Equality Vines Wine & Donate Benefiting SFM A Summer Gathering
  for Good\n\nSaturday\, August 15 | 4-7pm Equality Vines\, Guerneville\n\n
 Join us this summer for a relaxed afternoon of wine\, food\, and community
  with Equality Vines and Sonoma Family Meal - non-ticketed and open to all
  - in support of expanding food security and tuition-free culinary trainin
 g programs in Sonoma County.\n\nSip with a purpose as Equality Vines donat
 es 15% of all wine sales\, plus $5 for every bottle of Familia Tempranillo
  sold\, to Sonoma Family Meal. SFM's SABOR food truck will be onsite servi
 ng up fresh\, globally-inspired food for purchase\, and guests can enjoy o
 pportunities to learn about Sonoma Family Meal’s work\, participate in a
  raffle\, and connect over a shared commitment to community.\n\nCome sip\,
  savor\, and support - And see how doing good can taste good too!\n\nSonom
 a Family Meal is a local nonprofit employment social enterprise that has w
 orked to nourish the community and strengthen the local food ecosystem sin
 ce the tragic 2017 wildfires that left many people displaced and food-inse
 cure. Today\, our two kitchens provide over 7\,000 meals to those in need 
 each month\, while addressing food insecurity at the root through tuition-
 free culinary training programs that create opportunity and economic empow
 erment for low-income individuals facing barriers to employment or access 
 to education.
LOCATION:Equality Vines Tasting Room
URL:https://www.sonomafamilymeal.org/wineanddonate
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tomato Sagra: One-Night-Only Plant-Based Dinner with Little Saint 
 & A16
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T210000
UID:260719BNLYmgRbokyhjFGWrVWKRg
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, August 15 from 5–9 p.m.\, Little Saint\, the 1
 00% plant-based restaurant in Healdsburg\, and Michelin-recognized Italian
  restaurant\, A16\, are coming together for Tomato Sagra: A one-night-only
  plant-based dinner celebrating Southern Italian tradition and California'
 s peak tomato season. \n\nTomato Sagra brings together Chef Deborah Mulli
 n of Little Saint and Chef Valentin Atayde of A16 for a collaborative prix
  fixe dinner inspired by Southern Italy and Sonoma County's peak tomato se
 ason. Together\, the two culinary teams will showcase the season's juicies
 t\, sun-ripened tomatoes across a menu designed to capture the magic of su
 mmer. Imagine dishes like cold-cured olive misti with pickled cherry tomat
 oes\, oven-dried cherry tomatoes on the vine\, A16's signature Naples-styl
 e pizza\, and more — all featuring ingredients sourced from Little Saint
 's eight-acre regenerative farm.
LOCATION:Little Saint
URL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=1321324
 &restref=1321324&experienceId=764861&utm_source=external&utm_medium=referr
 al&utm_campaign=shared
