BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - Rails and Wheels
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T113000
UID:260526IMN4Vh7sGU212RqamUp-qQ
DESCRIPTION:**Turn of the Century Transportation**\n\nLearn about the Wild
  West days of both rail and auto transportation in Healdsburg and Sonoma C
 ounty in the late 19 th and early 20 th Century.\n\nMathew Lopez will tell
  tales of the cut-throat race to establish the San Francisco & North Pacif
 ic Railroad system in Sonoma County and its role in the formation of the m
 uch larger Northwestern Pacific Railroad.\n\nDon Anderson will focus on tr
 ansportation around town as it evolved from wagons\, livery stables and bi
 cycles to early automobiles\, commercial vehicles and buses. And how Heald
 sburg became an automobile-centric destination with the opening of the Red
 wood Highway.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
