BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Year of Horses Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T200000
UID:260730dRLgRDH7hke1WkxgTHfeFw
DESCRIPTION:**Saturday\, August 15th | 5 – 8 pm**\n\n The horse has car
 ried symbolic weight across cultures for centuries - a creature that embod
 ies freedom and strength\, loyalty and wildness\, grace and endurance. It 
 felt like the perfect spirit to gather around.\n\nJoin us Saturday\, Augus
 t 15th\, from 5 - 8pm at Pennyroyal Design in downtown Petaluma for an eve
 ning celebrating art\, craftsmanship\, and all things equestrian.\n\nArtis
 t Françoise LeClerc will debut a new collection of cyanotype prints and e
 questrian-inspired sculptures - work that explores strength\, vulnerabilit
 y\, and the quiet connection between horse and human.\n\nSacred Order will
  present a special collection of horse-inspired jewelry\, featuring new or
 iginal designs alongside thoughtfully curated antique pieces. Wendy's newe
 st horse-themed T-shirt will also make its debut\, perfectly complementing
  the evening's collection.\n\nWe'll also be unveiling Pennyroyal's first s
 mall collection of men's goods - a new chapter we're excited to share.\n\n
 We hope you'll join us as we celebrate the beauty\, symbolism\, and enduri
 ng spirit of the horse.
LOCATION:Pennyroyal Design
URL:https://pennyroyaldesign.com/blogs/news/year-of-the-horses-art-show
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:10 Things You Need to Know About Redwood Writers and Writing a Boo
 k
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T133000
UID:260729Zjm9sl_cRUeUdQFFZld56A
DESCRIPTION:**Are you looking for a writing club of nice people willing to
  help you write your first (or next) book?** Or are you new to Redwood Wri
 ters? We're Sonoma County's branch of the California Writers Club — and 
 as the largest writing club in California\, we support writers at any leve
 l. **Our mission is *writers helping writers*\, and we'd love to meet you.
 **\n\nThis month's gathering will serve as an introduction to Redwood Writ
 ers\, showcasing the many opportunities available within our branch and th
 e greater California Writers Club. You'll get a preview of the exciting ev
 ents and happenings planned for the year ahead — including our upcoming 
 **Sonoma County Writers Conference on October 17\, 2026** — along with w
 ays you can get more involved.\n\nWe'll round out the meeting with a few w
 riting exercises\, just to get the ink flowing.\n\nBest of all\, **if you 
 bring a friend\, both of you get in free!**\n\nBetter yet\, bring a friend
  and a dish to share when we network during the break.\n\nWe hope you'll j
 oin us and discover how Redwood Writers can inspire\, connect\, and suppor
 t you on your writing journey.
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Apple U-Pick at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T113000
UID:260729PZn-clHCX0ueE2PFduBTMw
DESCRIPTION:**Our popular Apple U-Pick Experiences return for a second yea
 r!**\n\nExperience the magic of harvest season at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
 \, where you can hand-select the most flavorful Honeycrisp or Fuji apples 
 straight from our certified organic orchard.\n\nTimed entries from 8:30am.
  Last orchard entry at 11:30am.\n\nAdmission: $8 for adults\, $3 for child
 ren. Registration required.\n\nU-Pick apples: $4 per pound.\n\n**Apple U-P
 ick FAQs** \n\nDo I need a reservation? \n\nYes! Please reserve your tim
 e slot on our reservation site. Reservations help us ensure everyone has a
  wonderful experience without overcrowding.  \n\nCan I show up without a
  reservation? \n\nWe require reservations to maintain our capacity limit
 s and ensure everyone enjoys their visit to the fullest.  \n\nCan I canc
 el my reservation?  \n\nAbsolutely! You can cancel your reservation up 
 to 48 hours before your scheduled time by calling us at 707-823-3100. Plea
 se note that cancellations made less than 48 hours in advance will result 
 in forfeiture of the entrance fee. \n\nCan I bring my dog?  \n\nDogs a
 re not permitted in the orchard\, with the exception of service animals. T
 his policy helps ensure the safety and comfort of all our visitors. \n\nC
 an I bring a stroller into the orchard?  \n\nFor safety reasons\, strol
 lers aren't allowed in the orchard\, but you're welcome to leave yours at 
 the check-in area where it will be safe and waiting for you!  \n\nI requ
 ire mobility accommodations. Can I still pick apples in the orchard?  \n
 \nYes. Please call us on 707-823-3110 once you’re made a reservation and
  we can provide suitable transportation into our orchard.\n\nWhy is there 
 an entrance fee?  \n\nThe entrance fee helps us maintain our beautiful 
 orchard and keep our experienced staff on hand to ensure everyone has a sa
 fe and enjoyable experience. \n\nHow much are the apples?  \n\nOur del
 icious U-pick apples are $4.00 per pound.  \n\nWhat variety of apples wi
 ll we be harvesting?  \n\nYou'll be picking either Honeycrisp or Fuji a
 pples (depending on seasonal availability).  \n\nCan I harvest heirloom 
 apples?  \n\nWhile heirloom apples aren't available for U-pick\, we off
 er many wonderful heirloom varieties for purchase in our Farm Shop.  \n\
 nAre your apples organic?  \n\nYes\, all our apples are organically gro
 wn and certified annually by Oregon Tilth!
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/u-pick
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mexican American Vintners Association's 14th Annual La Cosecha
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T210000
UID:260729PR8-_XDD5Ea76ncl8isbXA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Wine\, Culture & Community at the 14th Annual La Cos
 echa Grand Tasting\n\nJoin the Mexican American Vintners Association (MAVA
 ) for an unforgettable summer evening celebrating the vibrant spirit\, ric
 h heritage\, and exceptional craftsmanship of Mexican-American winemakers 
 at the 14th Annual La Cosecha Grand Tasting.\n\nSet against the beautiful 
 patio setting at Heirs of My Dream Winery in Sonoma\, this signature event
  brings together acclaimed MAVA member wineries\, culinary experiences\, l
 ive entertainment\, and community for an immersive wine country celebratio
 n unlike any other.\n\nSpend the afternoon tasting exceptional handcrafted
  wines from Mexican-American-owned wineries across California while enjoyi
 ng Latino-inspired cuisine\, live acoustic music\, and meaningful connecti
 ons with the vintners\, growers\, and families behind the labels. As the s
 un sets\, the evening transitions into an energetic after-party experience
  featuring live music\, dancing\, and continued celebration under the Sono
 ma sky.\n\nWhat Awaits You:\n\n🍷 Unlimited tastings from premier Mexica
 n-American-owned wineries\n\n🌮 Delicious Latino-inspired culinary offer
 ings and small bites\n\n🎶 Live acoustic music during the Grand Tasting\
 n\n✨ Meet the vintners\, growers\, and families shaping California wine 
 country\n\n🎁 Silent auction supporting MAVA’s scholarship and educati
 on programs\n\n💃 Live band and after-party celebration from 6:00 PM to 
 9:00 PM\n\n**Event Details**\n\nSaturday\, August 15\, 2026 4:30 PM – 9:
 00 PM PDT\n\nHeirs of My Dream Winery 22985 Burndale Road\, Buildings A & 
 B Sonoma\, CA 95476\n\nAttire: Wine Country Chic\n\n21+ Only | Rain or Shi
 ne\n\n**Event Schedule**\n\n4:30 PM – Grand Tasting Begins Enjoy unlimit
 ed tastings from Mexican-American-owned wineries\, culinary offerings\, li
 ve acoustic music\, and opportunities to meet the winemakers.\n\n6:00 PM 
 – After-Party Doors Open Guests who have purchased the After-Party Add-O
 n may enter beginning at 6:00 PM to enjoy live music\, dancing\, and an ev
 ening celebration of wine\, culture\, and community.\n\n6:00 PM – 9:00 P
 M – Live Music & After-Party\n\n7:00 PM – Grand Tasting Concludes\n\n9
 :00 PM – Event Ends\n\n**Ticket Information**\n\nGeneral Admission – G
 rand Tasting: $150 Includes unlimited wine tastings during the Grand Tasti
 ng experience from 4:30 PM – 7:00 PM.\n\nAfter-Party Add-On: $50\n\nCont
 inue the celebration after the Grand Tasting with access to the After-Part
 y beginning at 6:00 PM. Admission includes two glasses of wine and live en
 tertainment.\n\nAdditional food and beverages will be available for purcha
 se throughout the evening.\n\nDesignated Driver Ticket: $75\n\nWhether you
 ’re a devoted wine enthusiast\, an adventurous foodie\, or simply lookin
 g for a memorable evening in Sonoma wine country\, La Cosecha offers a rar
 e opportunity to experience the passion\, culture\, and innovation driving
  one of the wine industry’s most exciting communities.\n\n**About MAVA**
 \n\nThe Mexican American Vintners Association was founded to uplift\, supp
 ort\, and celebrate the contributions of Mexican-American vintners\, growe
 rs\, and industry leaders. Proceeds from La Cosecha help fund scholarships
 \, educational initiatives\, and year-round programming supporting the nex
 t generation of wine professionals.\n\n**Follow Along**\n\n@mava\\_wine | 
 #LaCosecha2026 | nsmava.org\n\n**Sponsorship Inquiries:** president@nvmava
 .org
LOCATION:Heirs of my Dream
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1990529001828/preview/?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
