BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T170000
UID:260212tk8wvOJ_JUylPk2F0dGCZQ
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nOvereaters An
 onymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on Sundays
  from 4:00 – 5:00 PM at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulupa Ave
 .\, Room \\#4\, Santa Rosa. Contact: Abigail \\(707\\) 293-5888. You may v
 iew all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbay
 oa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience spiritual\, emotional
 \, and physical recovery by practicing the Twelve Steps and living by thei
 r spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is not a diet club or ca
 lorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA d
 oes not endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is causing problems in 
 your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\, and
  help is available.\n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meetin
 g: https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Fools Journey Part 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260816T140000
UID:260728QwFCsLhViUqjDdPxNCfWoQ
DESCRIPTION:he Fool's Journey: Finding Yourself in the Major Arcana &mdash
 \; Part OneFrom The Fool to the Wheel of Fortune\n\nThe Major Arcana tells
  the story of the soul's journey through life. Beginning with the openness
  and possibility of The Fool\, we encounter teachers\, relationships\, cho
 ices\, challenges and opportunities that help shape who we are becoming.\n
 \nIn Part One of this two-part series\, we will explore the first half of 
 the Fool's Journey&mdash\;from The Fool through the Wheel of Fortune. Inst
 ead of memorizing isolated card meanings\, students will learn how these c
 ards connect to tell a larger story of identity\, growth and personal deve
 lopment.\n\nStudents will learn:\n\nHow the Major Arcana represents signif
 icant life lessons and turning pointsHow The Fool through the Wheel of For
 tune form the first stage of a symbolic journeyHow each archetype can appe
 ar in our everyday livesHow to recognize which Major Arcana energy they ma
 y currently be embodyingDuring our hands-on activity\, students will arran
 ge selected Major Arcana cards into the stages of the Fool's Journey\, exp
 lore how the story develops and identify the archetype that most closely r
 eflects their current chapter.\n\nThe Fool's Journey SpreadMy Current Arch
 etypeWhat Major Arcana energy am I embodying right now?My InitiationWhat i
 s this chapter of my journey trying to teach me?My Next ThresholdWhat ener
 gy am I preparing to step into?This beginner-friendly class will provide a
  framework for understanding the Major Arcana as a connected story rather 
 than 22 separate definitions. Returning students will also have an opportu
 nity to explore the cards as living archetypes and deepen their personal r
 elationship with the tarot.\n\nBring your favorite tarot deck\, a journal 
 and your curiosity as we gather for tea\, discussion and hands-on learning
 .
LOCATION:Songbird Community Healing Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/the-fools-journey-part-1?a
 ff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
