BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Savor Sonoma - Live Fire & Wine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T170000
UID:260724I3beW7W3aUOBoq9eNRpb4w
DESCRIPTION:Taste the very best of wine country. Savor Sonoma is an immers
 ive\, three-day flagship culinary festival. Over one spectacular weekend\,
  you'll explore five distinct experiences alongside national culinary star
 s and celebrated local artisans\, all set against the backdrop of open-fla
 me cooking and world-class Sonoma wines. Ignite your senses across two sp
 ectacular worlds. Step onto the pool deck\, where the rich aroma of live-f
 ire cooking fills the air and chefs plate flame-kissed proteins right befo
 re your eyes. Then\, wander inside to explore a vibrant Sonoma village pou
 ring celebrated local wines\, craft beers\, and agave spirits.\n\nFriday -
  The Headliners' Dinner at AYA:\n\n3:00 - 4:30 p.m. Meet culinary Legend A
 aron Sanchez\n\n6:00 - 7:00 p.m. Welcome cocktails and canapes\n\n7:00 - 1
 1:00 p.m. Five-course collaborative tasting with Aarón Sánchez\, Bryan V
 oltaggio\, Michael Voltaggio\, Charlie Palmer\, and Roy Ellamar\n\nSaturda
 y - Live Fire & Vine:\n\n12:00 - 1:00 p.m. VIP Early Access\n\n1:00 - 5:00
  p.m. General Admission Opens\n\n10:00 p.m. - 1:00 a.m. After Hours at AYA
 \n\nVIP Includes: Early VIP Entry beginning at 12:00 p.m. & an exclusive i
 nvite to AYA's After-Hours Party.\n\nImportant event info:\n\nMust be 21 o
 r over to attend and present valid ID to enter. No refunds\, no exchanges.
LOCATION:Graton Resort & Casino
URL:https://savorsonoma.com/#
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Goatlandia invites the Community to "Reggae to the Rescue!"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T170000
UID:260722xhJ0xNGViUax19dyCL9Wjg
DESCRIPTION:Party with a Purpose: Goatlandia Invites the Community to "Reg
 gae to the Rescue"—An Afternoon of Music\, Compassion & Farm Animal Fun\
 n\nSonoma County's favorite reggae band\, Sol Horizon\, headlines Goatland
 ia's biggest "fun-raising" celebration of the year on Saturday\, August 22
 .FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\n\nSEBASTOPOL\, Calif. — Goatlandia Farm Animal S
 anctuary & Education Center invites the community to trade the traditional
  black-tie gala for ﬂip-ﬂops\, island colors\, and good vibes at Regga
 e to the Rescue\, its annual fundraising celebration\, on Saturday\, Augus
 t 22\, 2026\, from 1:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. at the sanctuary's beautiful 36-
 acre property in Sebastopol. VIP guests are welcomed from 1:00–2:00 p.m.
 \, with General Admission beginning at 2:00 p.m. and continuing through 5:
 00 p.m. The event brings together live music\, rescued farm animals\, deli
 cious food and drinks\, and a shared commitment to creating a more compass
 ionate world. Event details are available at https://www.goatlandia.org/ev
 ents/reggae-to-the-rescue.\n\nHeadlining this year's celebration is Sol Ho
 rizon\, Sonoma County's beloved reggae band\, whose uplifting performances
  and loyal local following make them the perfect soundtrack for an unforge
 ttable afternoon of community and compassion. Guests will enjoy tropical-i
 nspired food from Goatlandia Kitchen\, local beverages\, time with the san
 ctuary's rescued animal residents\, games\, auctions\, and the joyful atmo
 sphere that has become a hallmark of Goatlandia's annual fundraising event
 s.\n\nUnlike traditional fundraising galas\, Goatlandia's annual celebrati
 on is intentionally designed to be welcoming\, relaxed\, and accessible.\n
 \n"Last year's theme was Peace\, Love & Goats\, and the response from our 
 community reminded us that people are looking for meaningful ways to come 
 together\," said Deborah Blum\, founder of Goatlandia. "With Reggae to the
 \n\nRescue\, we're celebrating compassion\, community\, and second chances
 —for animals and for people. We wanted to create a fundraiser that feels
  more like a joyful party than a formal gala\, where everyone can be part 
 of making a diﬀerence while dancing\, laughing\, and spending time with 
 our rescued animals. We are so grateful to our incredible community for ma
 king this work possible."\n\nProceeds from Reggae to the Rescue directly s
 upport Goatlandia's rescue\, rehabilitation\, and lifelong care of farm an
 imals while helping expand the organization's education programs that insp
 ire kindness toward animals\, people\, and the planet. The sanctuary has b
 ecome a beloved destination for families\, volunteers\, and visitors from 
 throughout Northern California seeking meaningful experiences that connect
  compassion with action.\n\nGuests are encouraged to wear their brightest 
 island attire\, bring friends and family\, and join Goatlandia for an afte
 rnoon where every ticket helps provide food\, shelter\, veterinary care\, 
 and hope for rescued farm animals.\n\nFor tickets and event information\, 
 visit\n\nhttps://www.goatlandia.org/events/reggae-to-the-rescue.\n\n Abou
 t Goatlandia Farm Animal Sanctuary & Education Center\n\nGoatlandia is a n
 onproﬁt farm animal sanctuary in Sebastopol\, California\, dedicated to 
 rescuing farm animals\, inspiring compassionate choices\, and creating mea
 ningful connections between animals\, people\, and the planet. Through res
 cue\, education\, community events\, and hands-on experiences\, Goatlandia
  provides a safe haven for animals while empowering people to live with gr
 eater kindness and purpose.\n\nMedia Contact\n\nDeborah Blum\n\nFounder\, 
 Goatlandia Farm Animal Sanctuary & Education Center Email: deborah@goatlan
 dia.org\n\nPhone: \\(707\\) 541-6216\n\nWebsite: https://www.goatlandia.or
 g
LOCATION:Goatlandia Farm Animal Sanctuary and Education Center
URL:https://www.goatlandia.org/events/reggae-to-the-rescue
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
