BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - Farm Town Forever
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T113000
UID:260526QxecX3HlSE-0_GbL0C3pvA
DESCRIPTION:**Dairy Farms & 4-H\, FFA and HFFCF Traditions**\n\nGrowing up
  in Healdsburg has often meant growing up with agriculture\, and that trad
 ition continues today.\n\nElizabeth Bucher\, who grew up on a dairy farm o
 n Westside Road\, will tell the story of how her immigrant family establis
 hed the farm and of the changes in the dairy industry in Sonoma County ove
 r the years.\n\nLillie Deas will give a hometown girl’s view of what it 
 means to grow up in a town that values agricultural education and culture\
 , with 4-H and FFA clubs and the annual Future Farmers Country Fair.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
