DESCRIPTION:Bring Your Own Tree Workshop\n\nBonsai Show at Redwood Empire 
 Bonsai Society\n\nAugust 22\, 2026 10am - 5pm\n\nAugust 23\, 2026 10am - 4
 pm\n\nhttps://www.rebsbonsai.org/\n\nBring your own tree \\(BYOT\\) with S
 am Tan Workshop Sunday 9AM - Noon\n\nLimited Space\n\nContact Bob Shimon\n
 \nshimon@mcn.org\n\nMEETING LOCATION\n\nGarden Room\, Rohnert Park Communi
 ty\n\nCenter\, 5401 Snyder Lane\, Rohnert Park\,\n\nCalifornia 94928\n\nBE
 GINNERS’ CLASSES\n\nREBS provides beginners classes in bonsai basics\, s
 cheduled periodically based on member and public sign ups. For a small fee
 \, students are introduced to the living art of bonsai. All materials are 
 provided and students get to keep their bonsai tree.\n\nMEMBERS’ WORKSHO
 PS\n\nREBS senior club members assist in styling\, care and maintenance of
  bonsai. These workshops are held monthly. Members work with their own bon
 sai\, tools\, wire\, and related materials. A small fee is required per wo
 rkshop.\n\nADVANCED WORKSHOPS\n\nAll advanced workshops are conducted by r
 enowned professional artists and instructors. These workshops are schedule
 d throughout the year.\n\nMEMBERSHIP\n\nFor additional information and mem
 bership form\, visit REBS website: https://www.rebsbonsai.org.\n\nCLUB INQ
 UIRIES\n\nEmail your inquiries to the following address: info@rebsbonsai.o
 rg
LOCATION:Rohnert Park Community Center
URL:https://www.rebsbonsai.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Nicolas Bearde
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T170000
UID:260508zYQeo_y9iEaGOT_DlEkyrQ
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Nicolas Bearde! Award winning recording artist\, Nicol
 as Bearde is a singer-songwriter\, actor and educator whose career has spa
 nned over 35 years. From his humble beginnings\, \\(born and raised in Nas
 hville\, TN\, the second of 7 children\\) to touring the globe with many o
 f today’s jazz legends\, Bearde has traveled many roads. His style is li
 kened to Lou Rawls\, Nat King Cole and Bill Withers and he is known for hi
 s “velvet voice”\, wit and engaging rapport that has drawn audiences i
 nto his live performances around the world.\n\nSonoma Sundays are free and
  open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the Sonoma Community Cent
 er\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNeely Family Foundation.\n\nPack 
 your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and meet us on the Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-8-23/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
