BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T211500
UID:2607168paPAShsJUSeR1coJ9mQ9w
DESCRIPTION:Bring a flashlight and your sense of wonder as you e
 xplore the park after dark. This hike heads up to the summit o
 f Bald Mountain\, where we will see the moon rise over the May
 acamas and the sun set over Sonoma Valley. This is a strenuous
  hike of approximately 6.5 miles with 1500\\+ of vertical and s
 ome steep sections \\(not recommended for children under 12\\).\n\
 nMeet at the White Barn parking lot at least 10 minutes prior 
 to the start time. Advance registration is $10 for general admis
 sion\, or $5 for youth \\(12-17 year olds\\)\, students\, Sugarlo
 af members\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers. All minors must be acc
 ompanied by a parent or legal guardian. You must register on th
 is page to attend\; tickets on site are $15 \\(exact change only
 \\) and might not be available. Bring your flashlight\, at least
  a quart of water\, snacks\, and extra layers for the evening.
  Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/aug2026moon-bald
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Holy Cow Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T213300
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T090000
UID:260715tEkrr6zomkitliZSf0sxNg
DESCRIPTION:Weekly Burner Radio Show at a variety of West County cultural 
 hubs. Local Dj WOLVERINE plus special guests perform three to 12 hour radi
 o show called Thee HOLY COW SHOW enumerating the greatness of BOB plus Psy
 chedelic treatment of popular bass music . Created and maintained at Burni
 ng man at BMIR at the Yearly Burning Man Festival . Plus 24/7 music on Sho
 utingfire.com . Always bringing in randomes for the show to sing\, talk\, 
 dance\, Dj or serve their master.
LOCATION:Kitty Kats Bangers Bus
URL:http://shoutingfire.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
