BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coming Home to Yourself A Self-Compassion Series with Horses
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T193000
UID:260713NU7wxGgQgEO0nWeGbm3kZw
DESCRIPTION:Coming Home to Yourself\n\nA Self-Compassion Series with Horse
 s\n\nThursday Evenings Open House: July 9\, 2026Series: July 16 – August
  27\, 2026\n\nNo Session on July 30th\n\nTime: 6-7:30pm\n\nComing Home to 
 Yourself  will be held at the Private Vacation Pasture of Heart & Mind E
 quine\, located on the border of Marin and Sonoma Counties\, along the 101
  freeway corridor\, close to the EarthRise Center at 101 San Antonio Road.
  Directions sent after registration.\n\nCome explore our self-compassion s
 eries with horses\n\nIn this series participants will interact with the ho
 rses to build trust\, establish boundaries\, and mirror the animals' prese
 nt-moment awareness\, helping to heal trauma\, reduce anxiety\, and improv
 e self-care.\n\nYour Registration Includes:\n\n- Six guided equine-assiste
 d self-compassion experiences\n\n- Facilitated group discussions and refle
 ction\n\n- Hands-on interactions with the horses\n\n- Workbook and between
 -session practices\n\n- Sound healing and breathwork exercises\n\n- Journa
 ling and creative expression activities\n\n- A supportive community of fel
 low participants\n\n- Ongoing opportunities to deepen self-awareness\, sel
 f-trust\, and self-care\n\nNo horse experience required\n\nLearn more abou
 t Heart & Mind Equine here: https://www.heartmindequine.com/
LOCATION:Heart and Mind Equine
URL:https://www.alanefreund.com/self-compassion-with-horses/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cooking Class with Sonoma Spice Queen Benefiting Sonoma Family Mea
 l
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T193000
UID:2606192yiG1SYMq0u7k_2JsFFkSQ
DESCRIPTION:Spice-forward Summer Spread: Cooking Class with Sonoma Spice Q
 ueen - August 27\n\n$125.00\n\nJoin us for another amazing cooking class w
 ith Sonoma Spice Queen\, learning all about how to create a spice-forward 
 summer spread for your outdoor\, hot-weather gatherings and celebrations.\
 n\nSonoma Spice Queen was started by spice enthusiast and culinary adventu
 rer Wind McAlister\, who also happens to be a huge Sonoma Family Meal supp
 orter \\(and our neighbor\\). Through her love of cooking and cultural exp
 loration\, Wind offers hand-crafted organic spice mixes and rubs\, with no
  fillers\, salt\, or sugar\, and is excited to be back to teach a second c
 lass in benefit of Sonoma Family Meal.\n\nThis hands-on\, collaborative co
 oking class will last 2.5 hours\, with time to enjoy your meal together at
  the end. Whether you’re a seasoned cook or just starting out\, our clas
 ses offer a fun\, engaging learning environment\, while raising funds for 
 Sonoma Family Meal’s free culinary job training and food-security progra
 ms.\n\nIf you haven’t been to the SFM Kitchen yet\, this class is also t
 he perfect chance to visit and experience where the magic takes place and 
 how the work gets done.\n\nWHEN: Thursday August 27th\, 2026\, 5-7:30pm WH
 ERE: SFM Community Kitchen\, 1370A Redwood Way\, Petaluma\n\nThe Menu:\n\n
 Curry Chicken Salad\n\nAsian Tofu Lettuce Cups with Chinese Five Spice and
  a coconut\n\npeanut sauce \\(vegan\\)\n\nStrawberries & Vanilla Bean Whip
 ped Cream served with a cookie\n\nLavender Lemonade
LOCATION:Sonoma Family Meal Community Kitchen
URL:https://www.sonomafamilymeal.org/store-2/cookingwithwind
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
