BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:H&L Live: Frank and the Bone Machine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T153000
UID:260728CglpwerqREipW1aw5EDCuA
DESCRIPTION:H&L Live: Frank and the Bone Machine\n\nFrank and the Bone Mac
 hine — a powerhouse North Bay ensemble celebrating the music of Tom Wait
 s.\n\nLed by musical director Paul Spina \\(drums\\)\, the group features 
 some of the region's most distinguished musicians: Jason Thwaits \\(guitar
 \\)\, Robby Elfman \\(sax\, clarinet\, keys\, and percussion\\)\, Ian Sche
 rer \\(guitar\\)\, Ben Dubin \\(bass and harmonica\\)\, and Devin Ruddick 
 \\(vocals\\).\n\nTogether they'll perform a hand-picked selection of their
  favorite cuts from across the Tom Waits catalog — a rare evening of sin
 gular music set against the backdrop of Sonoma County wine country.\n\n‍
 What to Know:\n\nAdmission is free - just show up and enjoy\n\nOutdoor se
 ating - lawn and picnic area available \\(bring blankets encouraged\\)\n\
 nAll ages welcome - family-friendly event\n\nWine available for purchase
  by the glass or bottle\n\nThis is H&L Live at its best: world-class music
 ians\, golden hour timing\, and the Russian River Valley as your backdrop.
  Come early\, stay late\, and experience why the North Bay music scene is 
 legendary.\n\n‍\n\n‍
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/hl-live-frank-and-the-bone-m
 achine
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Walk on the Wild Side – The World of Crepuscular and Nocturnal W
 ildlife
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T210000
UID:2607227swu4OpcZ0WOtAJTCx8yBw
DESCRIPTION:Experience Jack London State Historic Park in a whole new way 
 during Walk on the Wild Side\, a guided evening hike that reveals the fasc
 inating world of the park’s crepuscular and nocturnal wildlife.\n\nAs th
 e sun begins to set and the landscape transforms\, participants will take 
 a moderate-paced hike along park trails\, stopping periodically to learn a
 bout the animals that become more active as daylight fades. Along the way\
 , a park naturalist will share insights into the behaviors\, habitats\, an
 d adaptations of the wildlife that thrive during the evening hours.\n\nThi
 s educational hike offers a unique opportunity to experience the park’s 
 sights and sounds as day transitions to night\, while gaining a deeper app
 reciation for the wildlife of Jack London State Historic Park.\n\nThis eve
 nt includes an approximately 3.25-mile round-trip hike and is considered m
 oderate in difficulty.  This hike is recommended for participants ages 12
  and older. All minors under the age of 18 must be accompanied by an adult
 .  Please note that pet dogs (non-service animals) are not permitted on b
 ackcountry trails in order to protect wildlife.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/walk-on-the-wild-side/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
